1
00:00:47,777 --> 00:00:51,072
THE APARTMENT JOB

2
00:00:59,747 --> 00:01:01,499
<i>Then will you let me be the keeper</i>

3
00:01:02,125 --> 00:01:03,334
of your vault?

4
00:01:04,002 --> 00:01:07,547
You are the perfect man
to take on that position.

5
00:01:09,549 --> 00:01:11,342
MR. SON, SEOUL POLICE CHIEF

6
00:01:13,636 --> 00:01:14,804
Yes?

7
00:01:14,888 --> 00:01:16,306
<i>Hey, Mr. Park.</i>

8
00:01:16,389 --> 00:01:19,100
Did you know
Park Yong-man was terminally ill?

9
00:01:25,273 --> 00:01:26,441
What did you just say?

10
00:01:27,275 --> 00:01:30,320
They say it's pancreatic cancer.
He has about three months left.

11
00:01:30,403 --> 00:01:33,323
<i>You'd better hurry</i>
<i>if you don't want him to die in there.</i>

12
00:01:33,406 --> 00:01:34,407
<i>Get the ten billion.</i>

13
00:01:47,921 --> 00:01:50,840
I'm bringing over the ten billion,
so release him.

14
00:01:50,924 --> 00:01:51,925
Right now!

15
00:02:14,614 --> 00:02:16,699
<i>Uncle Hae-kang, here's a gift.</i>

16
00:02:17,242 --> 00:02:18,993
This is amazing.

17
00:02:19,077 --> 00:02:21,079
You could be an artist, Gyeong-buk.

18
00:02:21,788 --> 00:02:23,998
Is it really okay for me to have this?

19
00:02:24,082 --> 00:02:27,001
You're the head of our family, Uncle.

20
00:02:27,877 --> 00:02:29,587
<i>It seems like President Seo was taken out.</i>

21
00:02:29,671 --> 00:02:32,382
His entire family disappeared as well.

22
00:02:33,132 --> 00:02:35,843
<i>Then what did you see after failing?</i>

23
00:02:35,927 --> 00:02:37,971
This is my family.

24
00:02:39,764 --> 00:02:42,684
<i>We're a very happy family.</i>

25
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:46,980
Gyeong-buk!

26
00:02:55,488 --> 00:02:56,364
Wow!

27
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,449
<i>People.</i>

28
00:02:59,325 --> 00:03:00,535
<i>The people who are protecting me,</i>

29
00:03:01,619 --> 00:03:03,621
<i>and the people I should protect.</i>

30
00:03:29,856 --> 00:03:32,400
You crazy bastard. Are you kidding me?

31
00:03:33,067 --> 00:03:34,318
You said you'd bring the money.

32
00:03:34,402 --> 00:03:36,154
You were bringing the ten billion!

33
00:03:36,863 --> 00:03:39,907
That's why I had him moved

34
00:03:39,991 --> 00:03:43,202
to the hospital at this late hour.

35
00:03:43,286 --> 00:03:44,829
Do you think I'm playing around?

36
00:03:44,912 --> 00:03:47,373
All right. You just watch.

37
00:03:47,957 --> 00:03:50,877
You're the one
who's killing Park Yong-man.

38
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,670
Understand? You jerk.

39
00:03:53,963 --> 00:03:55,923
What the hell are you doing? Let go of me.

40
00:03:56,007 --> 00:03:57,175
The medical bail comes first.

41
00:03:57,258 --> 00:04:00,428
I told you, our deal comes first!

42
00:04:00,511 --> 00:04:02,305
The situation's changed.

43
00:04:03,222 --> 00:04:06,059
As you know,
he doesn't have much time left.

44
00:04:06,142 --> 00:04:09,312
That's why you'd better bring the money.

45
00:04:09,395 --> 00:04:11,939
Bring me the ten billion, you asshole!

46
00:04:13,566 --> 00:04:15,401
Let go of me.

47
00:04:17,111 --> 00:04:18,613
You'd better hurry,

48
00:04:19,947 --> 00:04:21,991
because that ten billion you want

49
00:04:23,534 --> 00:04:25,620
is on borrowed time too.

50
00:04:26,287 --> 00:04:27,163
Understand?

51
00:04:37,173 --> 00:04:39,217
PATIENT PARK YONG-MAN

52
00:05:03,699 --> 00:05:04,951
Yong-man.

53
00:05:05,618 --> 00:05:07,328
Hang in there.

54
00:05:10,957 --> 00:05:12,750
Hang in there just a while longer.

55
00:05:13,501 --> 00:05:14,419
Just a little more.

56
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:38,985
GUNAM TAESAN FACILITY MANAGER

57
00:05:46,909 --> 00:05:48,744
They received the money.

58
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:53,624
He needed the ten billion won
for his old boss,

59
00:05:54,458 --> 00:05:57,503
but he didn't take my money?

60
00:05:58,212 --> 00:06:03,050
Don't you think he has the potential
to be my vault keeper?

61
00:06:03,551 --> 00:06:04,719
I've been meaning to ask…

62
00:06:05,344 --> 00:06:07,763
Why Park Hae-kang?

63
00:06:14,395 --> 00:06:17,940
Stupid dogs only care about food.

64
00:06:18,024 --> 00:06:20,735
But once a smart dog is trained,

65
00:06:21,402 --> 00:06:23,654
it stays loyal to its owner.

66
00:06:25,072 --> 00:06:28,993
He planted relics
to stop the new town construction

67
00:06:29,785 --> 00:06:31,871
and doubled the reserve fund fee.

68
00:06:32,872 --> 00:06:34,248
Park Hae-kang

69
00:06:35,333 --> 00:06:37,960
can see the bigger picture.

70
00:06:43,507 --> 00:06:45,676
I heard you delivered the money safely.

71
00:06:46,802 --> 00:06:47,929
Thank you so much.

72
00:06:48,721 --> 00:06:50,556
But what brings you here at this hour?

73
00:06:51,390 --> 00:06:52,600
I remembered

74
00:06:54,060 --> 00:06:57,563
that we haven't discussed
a very important matter.

75
00:06:58,606 --> 00:07:00,483
What exactly…

76
00:07:02,276 --> 00:07:04,779
You've acquired someone more capable
than President Seo,

77
00:07:05,488 --> 00:07:07,865
so you should

78
00:07:09,325 --> 00:07:11,494
compensate me accordingly.

79
00:07:14,372 --> 00:07:16,916
We haven't discussed your payment.

80
00:07:17,458 --> 00:07:20,002
I'm not a cheap guy.

81
00:07:20,086 --> 00:07:23,172
We almost had a serious misunderstanding.

82
00:07:24,632 --> 00:07:25,675
Mr. Park.

83
00:07:26,509 --> 00:07:27,802
How much do you want?

84
00:07:29,262 --> 00:07:30,096
Ten billion.

85
00:07:32,014 --> 00:07:33,474
I want ten billion won.

86
00:07:38,646 --> 00:07:41,232
I've already doubled the reserve fund fee.

87
00:07:41,857 --> 00:07:44,610
So about 600 million
will be added to the fund each month.

88
00:07:45,361 --> 00:07:46,195
I believe

89
00:07:47,738 --> 00:07:51,117
I'm worth at least ten billion.

90
00:07:59,041 --> 00:08:00,668
Okay, fine. Ten billion.

91
00:08:08,718 --> 00:08:13,431
THE APARTMENT JOB

92
00:08:18,561 --> 00:08:20,271
Gyeong-nam, Je-gil, Big Guy.

93
00:08:23,566 --> 00:08:24,483
Guys.

94
00:08:26,319 --> 00:08:27,194
What?

95
00:08:29,363 --> 00:08:30,615
Guys!

96
00:09:00,853 --> 00:09:03,356
Come on.
Make a wish and blow out the candles.

97
00:09:03,439 --> 00:09:06,025
How many candles is that?

98
00:09:06,108 --> 00:09:08,152
-One, two, three…
-He's an old man now.

99
00:09:21,415 --> 00:09:23,084
That was a success.

100
00:09:23,167 --> 00:09:25,378
-Were you surprised?
-He was surprised.

101
00:09:56,951 --> 00:09:57,827
Did you cry?

102
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:01,205
No, I didn't cry.

103
00:10:01,288 --> 00:10:02,164
Never.

104
00:10:09,338 --> 00:10:12,341
They're the people
you want to protect, aren't they?

105
00:10:23,644 --> 00:10:26,689
Everyone's been saying that this place

106
00:10:26,772 --> 00:10:28,691
has an amazing sauna.

107
00:10:28,774 --> 00:10:30,025
Is it your first time here?

108
00:10:30,109 --> 00:10:31,318
Of course.

109
00:10:31,402 --> 00:10:32,778
I don't even live here.

110
00:10:33,279 --> 00:10:34,447
Then how do we get in?

111
00:10:35,030 --> 00:10:38,159
My friend lives here.

112
00:10:38,242 --> 00:10:39,869
I can just use her card.

113
00:10:40,745 --> 00:10:42,413
They don't even check your ID here.

114
00:10:42,496 --> 00:10:43,581
Come on.

115
00:10:44,457 --> 00:10:45,332
Unbelievable.

116
00:10:46,250 --> 00:10:49,587
So we've been paying the fees
while other people used our facilities.

117
00:10:49,670 --> 00:10:51,881
You saw the reserve fund fee, right?

118
00:10:51,964 --> 00:10:53,549
It's doubled now.

119
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:56,552
But doesn't it seem like the elevators

120
00:10:56,635 --> 00:10:58,220
are working fine now?

121
00:10:59,221 --> 00:11:01,098
It does seem so.

122
00:11:01,807 --> 00:11:04,518
But they should still be replaced
before any accidents occur.

123
00:11:05,686 --> 00:11:06,979
Ridiculous.

124
00:11:07,062 --> 00:11:08,898
Whose is this? Let me have a sip.

125
00:11:11,192 --> 00:11:12,443
I can't believe it.

126
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:15,613
Hey, did you know that there are people

127
00:11:15,696 --> 00:11:17,406
using our community sauna for free?

128
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:20,034
But we have to use our cards to enter.

129
00:11:20,117 --> 00:11:21,452
Yes.

130
00:11:22,244 --> 00:11:23,704
But some were just entering

131
00:11:23,787 --> 00:11:26,707
right after someone used their card
to open the gate.

132
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:29,126
And some are secretly lending them
to other people.

133
00:11:29,210 --> 00:11:32,254
I just heard there are rumors
that our sauna is good.

134
00:11:32,338 --> 00:11:34,757
My goodness.
Then they're using our sauna for free?

135
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:37,134
No way. It's not even that expensive.

136
00:11:37,218 --> 00:11:39,720
I just saw some people entering like that.

137
00:11:39,803 --> 00:11:43,265
If that's true,
this needs to be made public.

138
00:11:44,934 --> 00:11:47,394
REPORTING FACILITY MISUSE

139
00:11:54,568 --> 00:11:55,402
Please, eat.

140
00:11:55,486 --> 00:11:57,821
You probably had dinner,

141
00:11:57,905 --> 00:11:59,907
so I prepared some light snacks.

142
00:12:01,575 --> 00:12:03,202
We should make a toast,

143
00:12:04,620 --> 00:12:06,539
but the guest of honor isn't here yet.

144
00:12:07,206 --> 00:12:08,541
Please wait a moment.

145
00:12:09,291 --> 00:12:11,460
Is someone else coming?

146
00:12:16,215 --> 00:12:17,049
He's here.

147
00:12:21,262 --> 00:12:22,137
Say hello.

148
00:12:22,888 --> 00:12:25,516
Today's guest of honor, Park Hae-kang.

149
00:12:26,475 --> 00:12:28,060
You're here today

150
00:12:28,894 --> 00:12:31,397
thanks to Mr. Park.

151
00:12:33,691 --> 00:12:35,150
Say hello.

152
00:12:41,198 --> 00:12:42,408
Please, sit.

153
00:12:42,908 --> 00:12:43,867
Sit down.

154
00:12:45,703 --> 00:12:46,579
Go on.

155
00:12:52,209 --> 00:12:53,544
<i>So these two</i>

156
00:12:54,128 --> 00:12:56,171
<i>really were working for Lee Chung-won.</i>

157
00:12:56,255 --> 00:12:58,173
When President Seo was alive,

158
00:12:58,257 --> 00:13:00,718
I never got to prepare
a gathering like this.

159
00:13:00,801 --> 00:13:04,013
<i>Just how much influence does he have?</i>

160
00:13:04,096 --> 00:13:06,223
But we're a family now.

161
00:13:06,849 --> 00:13:09,935
So let's all line our pockets together.

162
00:13:14,815 --> 00:13:16,108
I'm joking.

163
00:13:17,818 --> 00:13:19,612
Why aren't you laughing?

164
00:13:22,906 --> 00:13:26,910
I'm just giving these out to you
because I'm in a good mood today.

165
00:13:26,994 --> 00:13:28,287
Hand them out.

166
00:13:41,008 --> 00:13:44,303
I gave you all an equal amount.

167
00:13:47,848 --> 00:13:48,891
See?

168
00:13:49,391 --> 00:13:52,269
Receiving gifts lightens the mood,
doesn't it?

169
00:13:52,353 --> 00:13:54,897
All right. How about a toast?

170
00:13:57,274 --> 00:13:58,817
Raise your glasses.

171
00:14:00,861 --> 00:14:01,904
Cheers.

172
00:14:02,488 --> 00:14:03,489
Cheers.

173
00:14:15,626 --> 00:14:16,460
I…

174
00:14:18,462 --> 00:14:22,049
You should have at least
told us in advance.

175
00:14:23,842 --> 00:14:25,135
It hasn't been long.

176
00:14:26,428 --> 00:14:27,680
What about you two?

177
00:14:28,222 --> 00:14:30,641
Ever since we started working here…

178
00:14:30,724 --> 00:14:31,850
Mr. Choi.

179
00:14:37,523 --> 00:14:40,109
Then I'll look forward
to working with you, sir.

180
00:14:49,493 --> 00:14:52,079
Were you faking a family to do this?

181
00:14:52,955 --> 00:14:53,872
What?

182
00:14:54,623 --> 00:14:56,041
Ha-jeong, what are you doing?

183
00:14:56,125 --> 00:14:57,876
I'm coming.

184
00:14:58,419 --> 00:14:59,920
You should stop this right now.

185
00:15:09,847 --> 00:15:12,975
When did Mr. Lee
get Park Hae-kang on his side too?

186
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:16,186
Whatever.

187
00:15:16,937 --> 00:15:19,314
It's not easy for people like us
to earn money.

188
00:15:20,274 --> 00:15:21,734
You know very well

189
00:15:21,817 --> 00:15:23,986
how much education costs, don't you?

190
00:15:24,945 --> 00:15:26,113
Yes.

191
00:15:27,781 --> 00:15:31,744
All I want
is to live quietly without any trouble

192
00:15:31,827 --> 00:15:34,997
until my kid graduates
from school in Canada.

193
00:15:36,331 --> 00:15:37,708
So please cooperate, Ha-jeong.

194
00:15:38,959 --> 00:15:39,877
Okay.

195
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:42,296
I'll get going now, Mr. Choi.

196
00:15:42,379 --> 00:15:43,964
Right. Bye.

197
00:15:57,644 --> 00:15:58,812
Kang Ha-ri.

198
00:15:58,896 --> 00:16:01,273
Quit that stand-in gig, right now.

199
00:16:02,399 --> 00:16:03,484
What?

200
00:16:03,567 --> 00:16:05,861
Do you even know what you've been doing?

201
00:16:05,944 --> 00:16:08,238
Do you know what kind of man
Park Hae-kang is?

202
00:16:09,448 --> 00:16:12,201
What about him? What's this about?

203
00:16:13,243 --> 00:16:15,496
You really are clueless, aren't you?

204
00:16:17,748 --> 00:16:19,291
What's gotten into her?

205
00:16:19,374 --> 00:16:20,626
Are you drunk?

206
00:16:43,982 --> 00:16:45,734
TRANSACTION LEDGER

207
00:16:52,241 --> 00:16:55,119
TRANSFERRED TO PRESIDENT SEO

208
00:17:10,008 --> 00:17:11,885
-Is it airtight?
-Yes.

209
00:17:12,719 --> 00:17:15,848
No one can tell by looking at the ledger.

210
00:17:15,931 --> 00:17:18,100
Of course. I know how skilled you are.

211
00:17:18,892 --> 00:17:20,686
Your sister's tuition is due soon, right?

212
00:17:23,814 --> 00:17:25,607
President Seo is very attentive.

213
00:17:34,533 --> 00:17:37,911
TRUE VALUE STATE
EXPENSE HISTORY

214
00:17:37,995 --> 00:17:39,913
FENCE REPAIRS
(MATERIAL COSTS OVERSTATED)

215
00:17:39,997 --> 00:17:41,415
LEAK REPAIRS
(CHARGED EXTRA)

216
00:17:44,918 --> 00:17:46,920
<i>How did things end up like this?</i>

217
00:17:52,551 --> 00:17:55,012
Attention, everyone.
We're all getting the same thing.

218
00:17:57,306 --> 00:17:58,765
Rotisserie chicken, 15 centimeters,

219
00:17:58,849 --> 00:18:00,642
grain bread with American cheese,

220
00:18:00,726 --> 00:18:02,144
heated in the oven,

221
00:18:02,227 --> 00:18:03,395
and leave out the pickles.

222
00:18:03,478 --> 00:18:05,522
Low-sugar onion and barbecue sauce.

223
00:18:06,273 --> 00:18:07,900
One, two, three, four, five…

224
00:18:08,650 --> 00:18:09,860
Six of them, please.

225
00:18:10,485 --> 00:18:12,321
-There are five of us. Why six?
-Yeah, why?

226
00:18:12,905 --> 00:18:15,532
It's tasty, so I'm getting two.

227
00:18:15,616 --> 00:18:16,909
Then one more for me.

228
00:18:16,992 --> 00:18:18,035
Me too. For Gyeong-buk.

229
00:18:18,118 --> 00:18:19,036
Me too.

230
00:18:20,245 --> 00:18:22,873
I need to send some to my family,
so five more.

231
00:18:22,956 --> 00:18:24,124
With all the ingredients.

232
00:18:27,461 --> 00:18:28,754
Fifteen, then.

233
00:18:29,338 --> 00:18:30,756
Fifteen?

234
00:18:32,382 --> 00:18:35,219
What? You met with the two of them?

235
00:18:35,761 --> 00:18:37,721
That's nerve-racking.

236
00:18:37,804 --> 00:18:40,098
Inviting you all together
to skim the fund…

237
00:18:40,182 --> 00:18:43,018
He really is something, isn't he?

238
00:18:43,101 --> 00:18:44,519
But the thing is… Come closer.

239
00:18:46,396 --> 00:18:47,689
The accounting manager

240
00:18:47,773 --> 00:18:50,442
knows that we're a fake family.

241
00:18:52,444 --> 00:18:53,278
How does she know?

242
00:18:53,362 --> 00:18:55,489
I'll get rid of her after I finish these.

243
00:18:56,865 --> 00:18:57,866
I'll hold back.

244
00:18:58,492 --> 00:18:59,618
She has a dirty secret too,

245
00:18:59,701 --> 00:19:03,205
so she won't be able to tell people
that we're a fake family.

246
00:19:03,288 --> 00:19:06,541
Ms. Jang, and now the accounting manager…

247
00:19:07,042 --> 00:19:08,794
Everyone will find out at this rate.

248
00:19:09,628 --> 00:19:12,673
We'll leave as soon as I get
the ten billion from him.

249
00:19:12,756 --> 00:19:13,715
-Yes, Boss.
-Yes, Boss.

250
00:19:14,299 --> 00:19:15,884
-Let's eat.
-Yes, Boss.

251
00:19:17,761 --> 00:19:20,138
Mr. Choi, you should see this.

252
00:19:20,639 --> 00:19:22,724
What is it this time?

253
00:19:23,350 --> 00:19:25,185
A complaint about people
using our facilities.

254
00:19:25,269 --> 00:19:26,937
REPORTING FACILITY MISUSE

255
00:19:27,562 --> 00:19:30,315
"Let's find out who they are
and shame them"?

256
00:19:30,399 --> 00:19:33,151
"Freeloaders." "Free sauna."

257
00:19:33,235 --> 00:19:35,237
"Security is too lax"?

258
00:19:35,821 --> 00:19:38,156
They're proposing
a facial recognition system.

259
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:42,744
Why is this leading to talk
about a facial recognition system?

260
00:19:42,828 --> 00:19:44,037
-No.
-No.

261
00:19:46,248 --> 00:19:47,916
Why would we spend needless money

262
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,211
just because
of a few irresponsible people?

263
00:19:51,295 --> 00:19:53,088
I'm against this.

264
00:19:53,171 --> 00:19:55,757
I think so as well,

265
00:19:56,383 --> 00:20:00,345
but more and more people
are agreeing to the idea.

266
00:20:01,263 --> 00:20:02,639
They want to use the reserve fund?

267
00:20:04,182 --> 00:20:05,892
-Yes.
-No…

268
00:20:05,976 --> 00:20:06,935
I mean…

269
00:20:08,145 --> 00:20:09,896
All we have to do is find the people

270
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:12,566
who are misusing our facilities
and give them a warning.

271
00:20:13,191 --> 00:20:15,193
Yes, that will be enough.

272
00:20:15,277 --> 00:20:18,071
Let's find them and expose them.

273
00:20:18,155 --> 00:20:21,658
If rumors spread about them,
they'll be too ashamed to do it again.

274
00:20:22,159 --> 00:20:26,455
But how would we find them?

275
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:36,923
All right. Good.

276
00:20:37,466 --> 00:20:39,009
Stop. Right there.

277
00:20:39,092 --> 00:20:40,552
The one with the pink basket.

278
00:20:40,635 --> 00:20:41,928
The elderly woman in the back.

279
00:20:42,012 --> 00:20:43,930
It's 12:54 and 7 seconds.

280
00:20:44,014 --> 00:20:45,932
…fifty-four and seven seconds.

281
00:20:46,016 --> 00:20:47,601
Check.

282
00:20:47,684 --> 00:20:49,186
It's Building 303, Unit 504.

283
00:20:49,269 --> 00:20:51,646
-Building 303…
-Unit 504.

284
00:20:51,730 --> 00:20:53,690
Unit 504. Okay, next.

285
00:20:56,401 --> 00:20:58,570
Still nothing from President Park?

286
00:20:58,653 --> 00:21:00,322
No, nothing.

287
00:21:00,405 --> 00:21:02,783
What about his brother?

288
00:21:02,866 --> 00:21:04,868
-Goodness!
-After drinking all that tea,

289
00:21:04,951 --> 00:21:06,078
he just ignores us?

290
00:21:06,161 --> 00:21:08,497
We even took his side
with the fee increase proposal.

291
00:21:08,580 --> 00:21:09,414
Right?

292
00:21:09,498 --> 00:21:13,001
This isn't right.
I didn't think he'd be like this.

293
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:16,088
Things were better with President Seo.

294
00:21:16,171 --> 00:21:17,798
It was nice being a building rep.

295
00:21:18,298 --> 00:21:20,133
We have to pay for heating bills now.

296
00:21:21,802 --> 00:21:24,346
And we're not getting any kickbacks.
This is no fun.

297
00:21:26,056 --> 00:21:28,683
Do we have to keep working
as building reps like this?

298
00:21:28,767 --> 00:21:30,519
What choice do we have?

299
00:21:30,602 --> 00:21:32,562
It's not like we can
bring Park Hae-kang down.

300
00:21:34,898 --> 00:21:37,651
Isn't there some clever way

301
00:21:37,734 --> 00:21:40,320
to bring Park Hae-kang down?

302
00:21:40,904 --> 00:21:44,241
Things have been noisy lately
about stopping unauthorized use

303
00:21:44,324 --> 00:21:45,158
of our facilities.

304
00:21:45,242 --> 00:21:46,243
Unauthorized use?

305
00:21:46,326 --> 00:21:48,370
Then let's at least go and sit

306
00:21:48,453 --> 00:21:50,455
in the management office, not here.

307
00:21:50,539 --> 00:21:53,083
Good idea.
Let's hang around there instead.

308
00:21:53,166 --> 00:21:55,252
I'm sure we'll find something.

309
00:21:55,335 --> 00:21:56,586
-Let's go.
-Really?

310
00:21:56,670 --> 00:21:57,838
-Get up.
-Okay.

311
00:22:00,507 --> 00:22:02,926
-Hello.
-Hello.

312
00:22:03,009 --> 00:22:04,177
Hi, Yun-seo.

313
00:22:04,261 --> 00:22:05,303
Hello.

314
00:22:06,638 --> 00:22:07,931
Is something wrong?

315
00:22:08,014 --> 00:22:11,351
We just wanted to chat
with the residents a bit.

316
00:22:11,435 --> 00:22:13,937
And since you're all working so hard,

317
00:22:14,020 --> 00:22:16,148
-we want to hear about your troubles.
-Right.

318
00:22:16,231 --> 00:22:17,566
We want to chat over some tea.

319
00:22:18,191 --> 00:22:19,484
I see.

320
00:22:19,568 --> 00:22:21,528
But Mr. Choi and President Park

321
00:22:21,611 --> 00:22:23,613
just went to check the security footage.

322
00:22:23,697 --> 00:22:25,240
Don't mind us. You can keep working.

323
00:22:25,323 --> 00:22:27,159
We have lots of time on our hands.

324
00:22:27,242 --> 00:22:29,911
-I'll make the coffee myself.
-Sure.

325
00:22:29,995 --> 00:22:32,873
But where are all the other employees?

326
00:22:33,790 --> 00:22:35,709
Everyone's busy.

327
00:22:38,170 --> 00:22:39,129
Yes?

328
00:22:40,005 --> 00:22:41,464
No one's there?

329
00:22:41,965 --> 00:22:43,216
Hang on.

330
00:22:44,092 --> 00:22:47,220
Building 105, Unit 702.

331
00:22:47,304 --> 00:22:48,305
It's a rental unit.

332
00:22:48,388 --> 00:22:50,891
Looks like
only elderly residents live there.

333
00:22:51,474 --> 00:22:53,476
Why don't you check in the afternoon?

334
00:22:54,144 --> 00:22:55,353
Okay.

335
00:22:55,437 --> 00:22:56,938
Building 105?

336
00:22:57,439 --> 00:22:58,940
That's where I live. What's going on?

337
00:23:00,650 --> 00:23:03,278
We're visiting residents

338
00:23:03,361 --> 00:23:06,781
who misused the community facilities
and giving them a warning.

339
00:23:06,865 --> 00:23:07,866
But they're not at home.

340
00:23:07,949 --> 00:23:10,660
I guess rental units
are misusing the facilities.

341
00:23:10,744 --> 00:23:13,371
They shouldn't do that
when they're living here for free.

342
00:23:13,955 --> 00:23:14,789
Pardon?

343
00:23:17,209 --> 00:23:18,418
No, it's not that--

344
00:23:18,501 --> 00:23:21,004
You seem busy. We'll come back next time.

345
00:23:21,504 --> 00:23:22,923
Right.

346
00:23:23,006 --> 00:23:25,133
I'll make my own coffee.

347
00:23:25,217 --> 00:23:26,760
-Bye.
-Bye.

348
00:23:27,469 --> 00:23:28,720
Bye…

349
00:23:34,559 --> 00:23:35,393
What is it?

350
00:23:35,477 --> 00:23:36,686
I think I got it.

351
00:23:36,770 --> 00:23:38,688
-What?
-Got what?

352
00:23:39,397 --> 00:23:40,273
A way…

353
00:23:41,358 --> 00:23:42,734
to drag Park Hae-kang down.

354
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:49,407
What is it?

355
00:23:49,491 --> 00:23:51,993
MOST FACILITY MISUSE
COMES FROM RENTAL UNITS…

356
00:23:53,703 --> 00:23:57,290
"Rental units should be limited
from using community facilities."

357
00:23:57,374 --> 00:23:59,709
"Rental unit beggars are the worst."

358
00:23:59,793 --> 00:24:01,878
"I'm struggling to pay
my mortgage interest."

359
00:24:01,962 --> 00:24:05,382
"It's infuriating how people
in the rental units have it so easy."

360
00:24:05,465 --> 00:24:07,342
"Reveal the rental units."

361
00:24:08,009 --> 00:24:10,136
What kind of nonsense is this?

362
00:24:12,514 --> 00:24:13,682
What a load of crap.

363
00:24:16,351 --> 00:24:18,186
I'm sorry, sir.

364
00:24:18,895 --> 00:24:22,190
I was just asked
who lives in Building 105, Unit 702

365
00:24:22,274 --> 00:24:26,236
because they weren't answering their door,

366
00:24:27,362 --> 00:24:29,656
so I said it was a rental unit.

367
00:24:31,366 --> 00:24:33,952
But the building reps who came
overheard me.

368
00:24:34,035 --> 00:24:38,540
I don't know why this led
to all the talk about the rental units.

369
00:24:39,541 --> 00:24:41,334
It's not something to apologize to me for.

370
00:24:42,127 --> 00:24:44,796
But you should apologize directly to them.

371
00:24:45,505 --> 00:24:47,465
They're moving out.

372
00:24:49,342 --> 00:24:51,011
CAN'T YOU EVEN PAY FOR A SAUNA?

373
00:24:51,094 --> 00:24:53,305
<i>This is a social mix apartment complex.</i>

374
00:24:54,097 --> 00:24:56,891
<i>The rental units and owner-occupied units</i>
<i>are mixed here,</i>

375
00:24:56,975 --> 00:24:59,686
<i>so the residents</i>
<i>couldn't know which units were rented.</i>

376
00:25:00,770 --> 00:25:05,317
But the residents acted as though
they had been waiting for this to happen,

377
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:08,236
so they seemed quite shocked.

378
00:25:09,070 --> 00:25:10,363
They said they just wanted

379
00:25:10,447 --> 00:25:14,117
to brag to their old neighbors
about living in a nice apartment complex.

380
00:25:14,826 --> 00:25:16,202
And here.

381
00:25:16,870 --> 00:25:21,082
They asked that this be used
for the apartment complex.

382
00:25:21,166 --> 00:25:22,917
And they apologized
for causing a commotion.

383
00:25:23,918 --> 00:25:25,462
It's the sauna fee.

384
00:25:37,390 --> 00:25:38,350
Here.

385
00:25:38,433 --> 00:25:40,018
Try another color too.

386
00:25:41,227 --> 00:25:42,771
Next color…

387
00:25:42,854 --> 00:25:44,147
Good.

388
00:25:44,230 --> 00:25:45,440
You're so smart.

389
00:25:45,523 --> 00:25:46,524
Draw one at the bottom.

390
00:25:46,608 --> 00:25:48,693
Wow, that's so cool.

391
00:25:48,777 --> 00:25:50,362
That's amazing.

392
00:25:50,445 --> 00:25:51,571
So cute.

393
00:25:52,781 --> 00:25:53,865
Who is this?

394
00:25:55,200 --> 00:25:56,910
-That's a nice rainbow.
-Is this Mom?

395
00:25:56,993 --> 00:25:59,913
What on earth are you doing right now?

396
00:26:01,706 --> 00:26:04,000
They're water-soluble crayons.

397
00:26:04,084 --> 00:26:05,460
It'll get washed away in the rain.

398
00:26:06,378 --> 00:26:09,547
This is still a public place.

399
00:26:09,631 --> 00:26:13,635
Are you seriously drawing
on a public building?

400
00:26:14,219 --> 00:26:15,678
We weren't…

401
00:26:15,762 --> 00:26:16,805
Oh gosh.

402
00:26:16,888 --> 00:26:20,141
Why do people here
have no sense of responsibility?

403
00:26:20,225 --> 00:26:23,144
Are you teaching your kids that it's okay

404
00:26:23,228 --> 00:26:24,771
to vandalize public property?

405
00:26:24,854 --> 00:26:27,982
We just told you
that it'll get washed away in the rain.

406
00:26:28,775 --> 00:26:30,151
Look.

407
00:26:30,235 --> 00:26:33,238
There's no forecast of rain
for a whole week.

408
00:26:33,321 --> 00:26:36,491
Then we can just spray water on it.

409
00:26:36,574 --> 00:26:37,992
And you can talk quietly.

410
00:26:38,076 --> 00:26:39,911
Why are you shouting
when there are kids here?

411
00:26:39,994 --> 00:26:43,373
So I guess you do feel embarrassed
getting called out in front of them.

412
00:26:43,456 --> 00:26:46,584
It's okay for kids to scribble sometimes,
and we said we'd erase it.

413
00:26:47,168 --> 00:26:48,670
You said the rain would wash it away.

414
00:26:48,753 --> 00:26:53,466
That means you had no intention
of erasing it before it rained.

415
00:26:53,550 --> 00:26:56,177
You should be the ones
stopping your kids from doing that,

416
00:26:56,261 --> 00:26:57,971
but you're doing it with them?

417
00:26:58,054 --> 00:27:00,390
Are you thoughtless or ill-mannered?

418
00:27:00,473 --> 00:27:01,683
Or just uneducated?

419
00:27:01,766 --> 00:27:02,725
You're unbelievable!

420
00:27:02,809 --> 00:27:04,519
-Did you hear that?
-Ma'am.

421
00:27:04,602 --> 00:27:05,812
You're being…

422
00:27:06,729 --> 00:27:07,981
What?

423
00:27:08,064 --> 00:27:09,816
Am I wrong?

424
00:27:09,899 --> 00:27:13,695
You young mothers
should have some sense of ownership!

425
00:27:13,778 --> 00:27:16,030
Is this really that big of a deal?

426
00:27:16,114 --> 00:27:18,783
We all have a sense of ownership!
We own our units!

427
00:27:18,867 --> 00:27:19,993
I'm an owner too!

428
00:27:20,076 --> 00:27:21,661
Right. Good for you.

429
00:27:21,744 --> 00:27:24,581
If you took out massive loans
to become owners

430
00:27:24,664 --> 00:27:26,666
of apartments like this,

431
00:27:26,749 --> 00:27:28,418
you should be thinking

432
00:27:28,501 --> 00:27:31,463
about educating your kids
and helping raise the property value.

433
00:27:31,546 --> 00:27:34,007
If rumors spread
about how bratty the kids are here,

434
00:27:34,090 --> 00:27:35,842
the prices will drop!

435
00:27:35,925 --> 00:27:37,177
-Hey!
-Hey!

436
00:27:37,927 --> 00:27:40,472
What? Why?

437
00:27:41,473 --> 00:27:42,390
-Gosh.
-My goodness.

438
00:27:42,474 --> 00:27:43,600
What's with that woman?

439
00:27:43,683 --> 00:27:44,976
As if she doesn't have any loans.

440
00:27:45,059 --> 00:27:46,978
Isn't there a way to find out?

441
00:27:47,061 --> 00:27:47,896
Is there?

442
00:27:47,979 --> 00:27:49,564
We can check the property registry.

443
00:27:49,647 --> 00:27:51,691
Anyone can view it
if you know the address.

444
00:27:51,774 --> 00:27:52,734
Really?

445
00:27:53,401 --> 00:27:55,570
She's in Building 112, right?

446
00:27:55,653 --> 00:27:56,696
Yes. Unit 902.

447
00:27:56,779 --> 00:27:59,282
We don't need to go that far.

448
00:27:59,365 --> 00:28:01,242
It's true that we drew
on a public building.

449
00:28:01,326 --> 00:28:03,453
We know it was our fault,

450
00:28:03,536 --> 00:28:05,872
but she was going on
about a sense of ownership

451
00:28:05,955 --> 00:28:08,082
and calling our kids brats
over something so trivial.

452
00:28:08,166 --> 00:28:10,543
We didn't need to hear
such harsh comments.

453
00:28:10,627 --> 00:28:11,586
You're right.

454
00:28:12,420 --> 00:28:14,589
She speaks so harshly.

455
00:28:14,672 --> 00:28:16,466
-She was spewing nonsense.
-Yeah.

456
00:28:17,425 --> 00:28:20,094
Let's sleep early today, okay?

457
00:28:20,803 --> 00:28:23,056
Mom, what's a loan?

458
00:28:25,892 --> 00:28:26,768
Well…

459
00:28:28,645 --> 00:28:32,065
It's when you borrow money from a bank
when you don't have enough.

460
00:28:32,690 --> 00:28:34,192
Do we not have money?

461
00:28:35,026 --> 00:28:35,985
What?

462
00:28:36,069 --> 00:28:38,154
That lady earlier

463
00:28:38,238 --> 00:28:40,323
said we had a huge loan.

464
00:28:46,246 --> 00:28:47,539
No, well…

465
00:28:49,541 --> 00:28:51,125
It's not huge.

466
00:28:52,919 --> 00:28:54,003
We have a bit.

467
00:28:54,587 --> 00:28:55,797
Just a little.

468
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:58,716
Hardly anyone buys an apartment
without a loan.

469
00:28:59,217 --> 00:29:00,885
She spoke as if she didn't.

470
00:29:05,807 --> 00:29:07,225
Should I check?

471
00:29:11,646 --> 00:29:13,982
What unit was she in again?

472
00:29:14,899 --> 00:29:16,901
Building 112, Unit 902…

473
00:29:16,985 --> 00:29:18,403
PROPERTY REGISTRY

474
00:29:20,530 --> 00:29:21,447
Oh my gosh.

475
00:29:33,751 --> 00:29:36,296
You have to do well today, okay?

476
00:29:37,046 --> 00:29:39,257
That sapling incident and the drawings…

477
00:29:39,340 --> 00:29:41,050
Remember everything she put us through.

478
00:29:41,134 --> 00:29:42,343
Too many to count.

479
00:29:42,427 --> 00:29:44,804
It's just ridiculous.

480
00:29:44,888 --> 00:29:47,891
Make sure she won't even dare
to say a thing.

481
00:29:47,974 --> 00:29:49,517
-Okay?
-Take her down a peg.

482
00:29:49,601 --> 00:29:51,060
You can do it.

483
00:29:51,144 --> 00:29:52,645
-We're relying on you.
-You can do it.

484
00:29:59,319 --> 00:30:01,446
TRUE VALUE STATE
RESIDENTS' ASSOCIATION MEETING

485
00:30:03,615 --> 00:30:07,410
Let us begin
the residents' association meeting.

486
00:30:07,493 --> 00:30:09,454
Today's agenda

487
00:30:09,537 --> 00:30:13,082
is how to prevent misuse
of the community center.

488
00:30:13,166 --> 00:30:14,292
Excuse me.

489
00:30:16,377 --> 00:30:18,755
Before starting the meeting,

490
00:30:18,838 --> 00:30:21,382
there's something I thought
you should know in advance.

491
00:30:21,466 --> 00:30:23,217
Let me announce something.

492
00:30:23,301 --> 00:30:24,719
For the past month,

493
00:30:24,802 --> 00:30:29,265
President Park and I have been staying up
all night reviewing security footage,

494
00:30:29,349 --> 00:30:33,394
checking the residents who have been
misusing the community center.

495
00:30:33,478 --> 00:30:37,273
We've identified a total of 108 cases.

496
00:30:37,357 --> 00:30:41,694
Four of them were from rental units,

497
00:30:41,778 --> 00:30:44,697
and the remaining 104

498
00:30:44,781 --> 00:30:47,492
were from purchased units.

499
00:30:48,618 --> 00:30:49,911
-Purchased units?
-What?

500
00:30:49,994 --> 00:30:51,996
That's way more than the rental units.

501
00:30:52,080 --> 00:30:54,415
The rental units
must have been pretty frustrated.

502
00:30:54,499 --> 00:30:56,960
Which purchased units
were being so thoughtless?

503
00:30:57,043 --> 00:30:58,252
Hang on.

504
00:30:58,336 --> 00:30:59,754
Are you sure about this?

505
00:31:00,380 --> 00:31:04,342
We visited each household to confirm this,
and they apologized.

506
00:31:04,425 --> 00:31:06,344
They promised not to do it again.

507
00:31:07,553 --> 00:31:09,013
So everyone,

508
00:31:09,097 --> 00:31:12,767
stop attacking the rental unit residents,

509
00:31:12,850 --> 00:31:15,353
and let us all get along--

510
00:31:15,436 --> 00:31:17,313
But, Ms. Jang,

511
00:31:18,189 --> 00:31:21,317
aren't you taking the rental units' side
because you're one too?

512
00:31:22,777 --> 00:31:24,028
-Rental unit?
-Ma'am.

513
00:31:24,112 --> 00:31:26,572
Everyone here lives
in an owner-occupied unit.

514
00:31:26,656 --> 00:31:28,533
Our management rules state

515
00:31:28,616 --> 00:31:30,868
that only those in owned units

516
00:31:31,494 --> 00:31:35,248
are able to participate
in the residents' association meetings.

517
00:31:35,331 --> 00:31:38,376
Then Ms. Jang should clearly leave.

518
00:31:38,459 --> 00:31:41,087
Because she doesn't own her unit.

519
00:31:42,130 --> 00:31:44,465
It's a rental unit
managed by the government.

520
00:31:46,509 --> 00:31:50,179
She always acted
like she had a say in everything.

521
00:31:50,263 --> 00:31:52,557
She spoke like that
when she's in a rental unit?

522
00:31:52,640 --> 00:31:54,642
-Wow.
-No wonder.

523
00:31:54,726 --> 00:31:56,728
She was always yelling at our kids.

524
00:31:56,811 --> 00:31:59,313
You were investigating stuff
and pretending to be a homeowner

525
00:31:59,397 --> 00:32:01,566
when you didn't have the authority?

526
00:32:01,649 --> 00:32:03,151
Hey.

527
00:32:03,818 --> 00:32:04,902
Pretending?

528
00:32:04,986 --> 00:32:08,740
That means she's been violating
our management rules.

529
00:32:08,823 --> 00:32:12,452
Residents from rental units
don't have the right to be here, so leave.

530
00:32:12,535 --> 00:32:13,703
She's right. Leave.

531
00:32:14,996 --> 00:32:16,289
Go.

532
00:32:18,541 --> 00:32:19,417
Get out!

533
00:32:19,500 --> 00:32:21,169
Hurry up and leave!

534
00:32:21,753 --> 00:32:22,754
Why?

535
00:32:26,257 --> 00:32:28,468
Why wouldn't I have the right?

536
00:32:30,553 --> 00:32:32,847
The government gave me the right

537
00:32:32,930 --> 00:32:37,018
to live here as if it were my own home
for 30 years without worrying.

538
00:32:37,602 --> 00:32:39,562
I don't pay as much as you,

539
00:32:39,645 --> 00:32:42,148
but I'm not living here for free.

540
00:32:42,732 --> 00:32:44,233
I pay the maintenance fees, the rent,

541
00:32:44,317 --> 00:32:46,652
and the government
pays for the reserve fund.

542
00:32:46,736 --> 00:32:50,031
I'm paying to live here too.
Why shouldn't I have the right?

543
00:32:52,492 --> 00:32:54,035
I don't own my house,

544
00:32:54,118 --> 00:32:57,330
but I lived with a bigger sense
of ownership than any of you.

545
00:32:58,247 --> 00:32:59,999
<i>It wasn't just my own house.</i>

546
00:33:00,083 --> 00:33:02,752
<i>I cleaned all around</i>
<i>the apartment complex,</i>

547
00:33:03,336 --> 00:33:04,712
<i>treating it as my own home.</i>

548
00:33:04,796 --> 00:33:09,509
Was anyone here more invested
in True Value's affairs than I was?

549
00:33:09,592 --> 00:33:10,635
Anyone?

550
00:33:12,053 --> 00:33:14,555
Building reps, say something.

551
00:33:14,639 --> 00:33:16,057
You have the title,

552
00:33:16,140 --> 00:33:19,352
but did any of you even care
if any electricity was being wasted

553
00:33:19,435 --> 00:33:21,687
or if any facilities were broken,

554
00:33:21,771 --> 00:33:24,315
causing danger to the residents?

555
00:33:24,398 --> 00:33:27,026
Did any of you even care
about things like that?

556
00:33:27,110 --> 00:33:29,278
Even so,

557
00:33:29,362 --> 00:33:31,030
you're still from a rental unit.

558
00:33:32,115 --> 00:33:33,950
Do I need some kind of qualification

559
00:33:34,033 --> 00:33:36,828
to want to make
the apartment complex I live in

560
00:33:38,246 --> 00:33:40,540
a better place?

561
00:33:41,666 --> 00:33:45,253
Just because
I'm a tiny bit poorer than you,

562
00:33:45,336 --> 00:33:48,339
am I supposed to shut up
and keep my head down?

563
00:33:49,382 --> 00:33:50,925
Management rules?

564
00:33:51,425 --> 00:33:54,929
What kind of stupid management rules
are like that?

565
00:33:56,931 --> 00:33:57,890
How…

566
00:33:59,016 --> 00:34:00,685
How could you treat people like that?

567
00:34:00,768 --> 00:34:02,645
Oh, whatever.

568
00:34:02,728 --> 00:34:04,438
It's still against the rules.

569
00:34:04,522 --> 00:34:05,857
It's clearly stated.

570
00:34:05,940 --> 00:34:08,234
-This is wrong.
-We should follow procedure.

571
00:34:08,317 --> 00:34:10,153
-We should stick to…
-Stop.

572
00:34:59,911 --> 00:35:01,495
Sir! Be careful!

573
00:35:01,579 --> 00:35:02,955
Be careful not to scratch anything.

574
00:35:03,039 --> 00:35:04,916
-To the right.
-This way.

575
00:35:04,999 --> 00:35:06,584
Don't put it there.

576
00:35:06,667 --> 00:35:10,588
You have to place them on the mat.
Don't put them on the floor.

577
00:35:11,088 --> 00:35:13,090
You moved to a nice place, ma'am.

578
00:35:14,759 --> 00:35:16,802
It's a new apartment.

579
00:35:18,596 --> 00:35:20,181
No need for such formality.

580
00:35:22,475 --> 00:35:23,768
I really

581
00:35:24,393 --> 00:35:27,521
don't need to worry about a house anymore!

582
00:35:31,317 --> 00:35:35,905
This will be my home for 30 years.

583
00:35:36,656 --> 00:35:40,368
So I guess I can call myself the owner.

584
00:35:43,120 --> 00:35:47,166
I'll be relying on you, elevator.

585
00:36:23,160 --> 00:36:26,289
Did you have to bring that up
in front of everyone?

586
00:36:30,334 --> 00:36:32,753
It just seemed
like you wanted to humiliate her.

587
00:36:33,337 --> 00:36:34,463
Was that your intention?

588
00:36:37,008 --> 00:36:39,885
I was rash.

589
00:36:40,803 --> 00:36:42,179
I'm sorry.

590
00:36:44,181 --> 00:36:48,978
You should be apologizing
to Ms. Jang, not me.

591
00:36:54,567 --> 00:36:57,570
I really can't believe that Ms. Jang

592
00:36:57,653 --> 00:36:59,238
is in a rental unit.

593
00:37:00,823 --> 00:37:05,161
You should've checked when she applied
as a building rep candidate.

594
00:37:05,244 --> 00:37:07,872
You really didn't know, Mr. Choi?

595
00:37:08,497 --> 00:37:09,707
I didn't.

596
00:37:10,207 --> 00:37:12,877
She was meddling in everything,

597
00:37:12,960 --> 00:37:14,920
so of course I thought she owned her unit.

598
00:37:15,004 --> 00:37:17,256
Who would've imagined
it was a rental unit?

599
00:37:17,340 --> 00:37:19,133
She stuck her nose into everything.

600
00:37:20,092 --> 00:37:22,720
Sang-tae, don't talk about her like that.

601
00:37:23,304 --> 00:37:26,140
How can you say that
after hearing everything she said?

602
00:37:27,308 --> 00:37:29,101
I was just…

603
00:37:29,185 --> 00:37:33,147
Ms. Jang even went around
scraping gum off the ground.

604
00:37:33,230 --> 00:37:34,273
Yeah.

605
00:37:34,357 --> 00:37:38,486
Ms. Jang loves and cares for True Value

606
00:37:38,569 --> 00:37:40,196
more than any of the owners.

607
00:37:52,208 --> 00:37:53,042
Mom.

608
00:37:53,584 --> 00:37:55,211
I might get a scholarship this semester.

609
00:37:56,253 --> 00:37:57,171
Okay.

610
00:38:15,815 --> 00:38:16,649
Mom.

611
00:38:17,191 --> 00:38:19,360
Even if we don't own this house,

612
00:38:20,569 --> 00:38:22,905
I've been really happy living here.

613
00:38:25,533 --> 00:38:28,327
So I wondered why I was so happy,

614
00:38:28,911 --> 00:38:31,288
and it was because of you, not this house.

615
00:38:32,665 --> 00:38:34,125
Because you're happy.

616
00:38:36,252 --> 00:38:37,086
Mom.

617
00:38:37,837 --> 00:38:39,338
The house isn't what's important.

618
00:38:41,006 --> 00:38:43,467
What matters is the happiness
of the people living there.

619
00:38:50,599 --> 00:38:51,934
I'm going to school now.

620
00:39:17,251 --> 00:39:18,586
This place is good.

621
00:39:20,087 --> 00:39:23,424
I'm sure you didn't call me
just to enjoy a nice meal.

622
00:39:23,924 --> 00:39:27,511
Why did you want to see me?

623
00:39:28,304 --> 00:39:31,640
Well, it's about
the Oman New Town project.

624
00:39:31,724 --> 00:39:35,019
We need to add more rental units
than we originally planned.

625
00:39:38,814 --> 00:39:41,025
-Why?
-Isn't it obvious?

626
00:39:41,108 --> 00:39:44,028
The VIP is pursuing policies
for ordinary people,

627
00:39:44,111 --> 00:39:46,822
so he wants to show off

628
00:39:46,906 --> 00:39:49,658
about adding more rental units
in the new town.

629
00:39:51,577 --> 00:39:53,329
Increasing housing supply

630
00:39:53,412 --> 00:39:58,042
while supporting vulnerable groups…

631
00:39:58,918 --> 00:40:00,169
It creates a good image.

632
00:40:06,967 --> 00:40:09,345
Did they replace the head chef?

633
00:40:09,428 --> 00:40:11,597
Why does it feel like I'm chewing on sand?

634
00:40:16,227 --> 00:40:17,728
Are you enjoying the food?

635
00:40:18,646 --> 00:40:20,564
You have quite the stomach,

636
00:40:20,648 --> 00:40:23,734
enjoying it
after the bomb you threw at me.

637
00:40:31,951 --> 00:40:33,035
Have a drink.

638
00:41:03,691 --> 00:41:07,111
An apartment costs a fortune,
and they want them for free?

639
00:41:08,279 --> 00:41:10,864
The government
is basically extorting money from me.

640
00:41:10,948 --> 00:41:12,575
Are they thugs or what?

641
00:41:14,159 --> 00:41:15,536
Damn rental units…

642
00:41:16,328 --> 00:41:18,205
I want to get rid of them all.

643
00:41:22,543 --> 00:41:24,712
TRUE VALUE FACILITY MANAGER

644
00:41:26,380 --> 00:41:27,464
What is it?

645
00:41:28,132 --> 00:41:31,260
You told me to report to you
every two days.

646
00:41:32,761 --> 00:41:33,887
Go on.

647
00:41:34,388 --> 00:41:36,599
<i>It's been kind of noisy here</i>

648
00:41:36,682 --> 00:41:40,769
with conflict between the rental units
and owned units

649
00:41:40,853 --> 00:41:43,272
surrounding the misuse
of community facilities.

650
00:41:43,355 --> 00:41:47,276
<i>President Park is probably getting</i>
<i>quite a headache because of this.</i>

651
00:41:48,152 --> 00:41:51,405
Rental units always seem
to be the problem.

652
00:41:58,996 --> 00:42:01,332
Give me back my apartments, you thieves!

653
00:42:01,415 --> 00:42:03,375
Are you thugs or what?

654
00:42:17,723 --> 00:42:19,350
Why did you call me at this hour?

655
00:42:19,975 --> 00:42:22,645
Drink this. It's good for your health.

656
00:42:31,403 --> 00:42:35,240
I heard you're having trouble
with the rental units.

657
00:42:36,325 --> 00:42:39,078
I'm pretty irritated because of them too.

658
00:42:40,537 --> 00:42:42,081
It's not really them,

659
00:42:42,164 --> 00:42:44,500
but the way people view them.

660
00:42:45,084 --> 00:42:47,211
Whatever the case,

661
00:42:47,294 --> 00:42:49,797
the rental units are the problem.

662
00:42:50,422 --> 00:42:51,548
The government

663
00:42:51,632 --> 00:42:54,259
wants my apartments for free.

664
00:42:54,802 --> 00:42:56,553
I gave them some, but they want more.

665
00:42:57,262 --> 00:42:58,889
They act as if they own them.

666
00:43:00,099 --> 00:43:03,811
They want to steal mine
and give them out as rental units,

667
00:43:04,395 --> 00:43:07,564
so it's only natural
for the owner to be pissed.

668
00:43:08,982 --> 00:43:11,652
The conflict between
the owned units and rental units…

669
00:43:12,528 --> 00:43:14,363
Right. Conflict.

670
00:43:15,989 --> 00:43:19,410
Should we just start a war between them?

671
00:43:19,993 --> 00:43:23,706
There's nothing more entertaining
than watching a fight.

672
00:43:25,499 --> 00:43:29,545
"Social mix." That's exactly the kind
of policy dreamed up by bureaucrats.

673
00:43:29,628 --> 00:43:32,172
People from different social classes
living together?

674
00:43:32,256 --> 00:43:34,508
Isn't that some kind of pipe dream?

675
00:43:35,342 --> 00:43:37,511
Let's be honest.

676
00:43:39,596 --> 00:43:42,933
Why don't we just mark the rental units

677
00:43:43,016 --> 00:43:44,643
with signs on their doors?

678
00:43:45,894 --> 00:43:48,689
You need to know
who your opponents are to fight them.

679
00:43:49,356 --> 00:43:50,190
Right?

680
00:43:52,901 --> 00:43:53,819
Never mind.

681
00:43:55,028 --> 00:43:58,282
There's no need for the staff
to do so much work.

682
00:43:59,700 --> 00:44:00,743
Just…

683
00:44:02,786 --> 00:44:05,289
reveal all the rental units, Mr. Park.

684
00:44:06,290 --> 00:44:09,460
I'm preparing the ten billion
that I promised you.

685
00:44:09,543 --> 00:44:13,297
But I need some time
to gather that much cash.

686
00:44:16,008 --> 00:44:19,261
If you reveal all the rental units,

687
00:44:20,804 --> 00:44:23,223
I could get it prepared faster.

688
00:44:32,691 --> 00:44:34,234
Did you add eggs?

689
00:44:34,860 --> 00:44:35,986
Eggs are expensive.

690
00:44:36,069 --> 00:44:37,613
There's only enough for Gyeong-buk.

691
00:44:37,696 --> 00:44:39,239
Hey, what about me?

692
00:44:39,323 --> 00:44:41,241
Elderly people need protein as well.

693
00:44:41,325 --> 00:44:42,534
I'll eat them then.

694
00:44:42,618 --> 00:44:44,453
Sure. I need carbs too.

695
00:44:44,536 --> 00:44:46,371
-You're back.
-Yes.

696
00:44:47,831 --> 00:44:49,082
Ms. Kang, you're still here.

697
00:44:50,125 --> 00:44:51,460
I'm going now.

698
00:44:51,543 --> 00:44:53,587
She must have been waiting for him.

699
00:44:53,670 --> 00:44:56,089
She must've missed him all day.

700
00:44:56,173 --> 00:44:58,592
You know I can hear you. I'm leaving now.

701
00:45:00,844 --> 00:45:01,845
Bye.

702
00:45:02,638 --> 00:45:03,680
Get home safely.

703
00:45:03,764 --> 00:45:05,474
Did you eat, Boss?

704
00:45:07,392 --> 00:45:08,644
MANAGEMENT REGULATIONS

705
00:45:12,814 --> 00:45:15,275
Ms. Kang, can you work overtime today?

706
00:45:19,112 --> 00:45:20,614
"Overtime."

707
00:45:20,697 --> 00:45:22,449
I can't believe that sounds so sweet.

708
00:45:22,533 --> 00:45:24,368
I think my heart is working overtime.

709
00:45:26,036 --> 00:45:28,455
This is the Special Act
on Private Rental Housing.

710
00:45:28,539 --> 00:45:32,292
Paragraph 2 states you can form
a council of lessees' representatives.

711
00:45:32,376 --> 00:45:34,419
But this regulation book
was made by the developer

712
00:45:34,503 --> 00:45:36,880
when the residents first moved in,

713
00:45:36,964 --> 00:45:38,924
and it's never been revised.

714
00:45:39,967 --> 00:45:41,885
But I don't understand this part.

715
00:45:41,969 --> 00:45:44,846
This part in the regulations.

716
00:45:44,930 --> 00:45:45,931
What about this?

717
00:45:47,182 --> 00:45:48,475
A love story…

718
00:45:49,893 --> 00:45:51,728
Big Guy, what are you doing?

719
00:45:52,354 --> 00:45:53,772
Should we get them some snacks?

720
00:45:53,855 --> 00:45:55,065
It's not the time for that.

721
00:45:56,316 --> 00:45:58,235
We should give them some privacy.

722
00:45:58,819 --> 00:45:59,653
Close the door.

723
00:46:04,366 --> 00:46:05,784
What are they doing?

724
00:46:07,035 --> 00:46:08,745
-Do you need anything?
-Sorry!

725
00:46:10,747 --> 00:46:11,582
Are you okay?

726
00:46:12,666 --> 00:46:14,334
Aren't you bleeding?

727
00:46:15,460 --> 00:46:16,587
So…

728
00:46:18,880 --> 00:46:19,881
Get out!

729
00:46:20,382 --> 00:46:21,466
Forgot this.

730
00:46:22,718 --> 00:46:23,635
Seriously…

731
00:46:34,229 --> 00:46:35,439
What brings you here?

732
00:46:36,231 --> 00:46:37,441
I have something to tell you.

733
00:46:38,942 --> 00:46:39,776
Sure.

734
00:46:45,699 --> 00:46:46,533
Ms. Jang.

735
00:46:47,951 --> 00:46:49,995
I need you to quit.

736
00:46:56,877 --> 00:46:58,712
You too?

737
00:47:01,256 --> 00:47:02,924
Quit your role as Senior Secretary.

738
00:47:03,592 --> 00:47:04,718
How about managing

739
00:47:05,218 --> 00:47:07,804
apartment affairs with me
as another president?

740
00:47:09,264 --> 00:47:11,433
So with the revision
to the rental housing laws,

741
00:47:11,516 --> 00:47:13,894
tenants in rental housing complexes
with 150 or more units

742
00:47:13,977 --> 00:47:16,855
should have formed
a tenants' representative council.

743
00:47:16,938 --> 00:47:17,773
That's right.

744
00:47:17,856 --> 00:47:20,442
But there are 1,200 rental units here.

745
00:47:20,525 --> 00:47:21,985
Why hasn't one been formed?

746
00:47:23,612 --> 00:47:24,613
We can make one now.

747
00:47:25,113 --> 00:47:28,492
We're going to form
a tenants' representative council.

748
00:47:29,201 --> 00:47:32,913
There's a tenants' representative council?

749
00:47:33,580 --> 00:47:37,000
True Value's regulations don't state
anything about a tenants' council.

750
00:47:37,084 --> 00:47:39,961
I'll correct any wrong
management regulations here.

751
00:47:40,045 --> 00:47:42,297
According to the Special Act
on Public Housing

752
00:47:42,381 --> 00:47:45,384
and the Special Act
on Private Rental Housing,

753
00:47:45,967 --> 00:47:49,930
rental housing residents may also form
a representative council.

754
00:47:50,722 --> 00:47:52,265
Why don't you step up for this?

755
00:47:54,685 --> 00:47:55,519
Me?

756
00:47:56,103 --> 00:47:57,312
From now on,

757
00:47:57,396 --> 00:48:01,108
make your voice heard
as a representative of the tenants.

758
00:48:03,151 --> 00:48:04,695
President Park…

759
00:48:10,492 --> 00:48:12,786
TENANTS' COUNCIL
BUILDING REPRESENTATIVE ELECTION

760
00:48:12,869 --> 00:48:15,789
Mr. Park, you're smarter than I thought.

761
00:48:16,873 --> 00:48:18,458
It's all thanks to our overtime work.

762
00:48:18,542 --> 00:48:20,252
Don't forget my overtime pay.

763
00:48:24,131 --> 00:48:25,048
CANDIDATE PROFILE

764
00:48:25,132 --> 00:48:27,592
<i>Jang Suk-jin can do a great job</i>

765
00:48:27,676 --> 00:48:30,929
I'm running for tenants' representative.

766
00:48:31,012 --> 00:48:32,931
We're holding an election. Please read it.

767
00:48:33,014 --> 00:48:34,391
I'm Jang Suk-jin.

768
00:48:34,474 --> 00:48:35,517
Candidate 1, Jang Suk-jin.

769
00:48:35,600 --> 00:48:37,561
-I'm a candidate.
-A tenants' rep?

770
00:48:37,644 --> 00:48:41,064
We need tenants' representatives
to improve the apartment.

771
00:48:41,148 --> 00:48:42,691
DON'T IGNORE THE RIGHTS
OF 1,200 HOUSEHOLDS

772
00:48:42,774 --> 00:48:44,526
Hello, please take a look.

773
00:48:45,235 --> 00:48:46,570
We're electing tenants' reps.

774
00:48:46,653 --> 00:48:49,239
Candidate 1, Jang Suk-jin.

775
00:48:49,322 --> 00:48:50,240
You may begin.

776
00:48:53,660 --> 00:48:54,828
Hello.

777
00:48:55,746 --> 00:48:58,582
I'm Candidate 1
for building representative

778
00:48:59,249 --> 00:49:01,835
on the tenants' council, Jang Suk-jin.

779
00:49:02,419 --> 00:49:05,255
I live in a rental unit.

780
00:49:05,922 --> 00:49:08,550
I can't believe I got selected.

781
00:49:08,633 --> 00:49:11,762
<i>I'm enjoying the comfort</i>
<i>and happiness of True Value</i>

782
00:49:11,845 --> 00:49:14,556
<i>for a small amount of money.</i>

783
00:49:15,515 --> 00:49:16,683
Hello.

784
00:49:17,184 --> 00:49:19,269
It's a rental unit
managed by the government.

785
00:49:21,021 --> 00:49:24,441
<i>I understand the sense of superiority</i>
<i>that some homeowners have.</i>

786
00:49:25,484 --> 00:49:27,819
You've worked extremely hard,

787
00:49:27,903 --> 00:49:29,696
mortgaged your futures,

788
00:49:29,780 --> 00:49:33,325
and sacrificed other chances at happiness

789
00:49:33,408 --> 00:49:35,786
to buy your apartments.

790
00:49:37,329 --> 00:49:40,499
<i>However, I would like to ask you</i>

791
00:49:40,582 --> 00:49:44,795
to acknowledge the residents
in rental units

792
00:49:44,878 --> 00:49:47,547
as a part of True Value's community.

793
00:49:48,298 --> 00:49:51,760
<i>We do not wish to live here</i>

794
00:49:51,843 --> 00:49:55,639
<i>as shameful parasites</i>
<i>living off True Value.</i>

795
00:49:55,722 --> 00:49:59,643
I would like to live here proudly
as a resident of a rental unit,

796
00:49:59,726 --> 00:50:02,771
enjoying my freedom
and fulfilling my responsibilities.

797
00:50:03,396 --> 00:50:04,397
Anyone here?

798
00:50:04,898 --> 00:50:05,816
Light's still on.

799
00:50:05,899 --> 00:50:08,318
<i>I will take on the responsibility</i>

800
00:50:08,401 --> 00:50:11,863
<i>of caring for and protecting</i>
<i>the facilities of this community</i>

801
00:50:11,947 --> 00:50:14,407
<i>as if they were my own.</i>

802
00:50:15,325 --> 00:50:16,618
Here.

803
00:50:18,662 --> 00:50:20,247
I, Jang Suk-jin,

804
00:50:20,789 --> 00:50:22,749
will represent the tenants

805
00:50:22,833 --> 00:50:25,627
and do my best to cooperate
with the homeowners

806
00:50:25,710 --> 00:50:29,673
to create a better environment
at True Value.

807
00:50:30,590 --> 00:50:31,591
Thank you.

808
00:50:40,684 --> 00:50:43,520
I TOTALLY AGREE WITH YOU…
I HOPE YOU GET ELECTED!

809
00:50:45,146 --> 00:50:46,439
"I support you."

810
00:50:48,733 --> 00:50:50,443
"Thank you."

811
00:50:51,945 --> 00:50:53,238
I'm so grateful.

812
00:50:58,618 --> 00:51:01,329
PRESIDENT JANG SUK-JIN
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR APPOINTMENT!

813
00:51:01,413 --> 00:51:04,165
-Congratulations.
-Congratulations.

814
00:51:04,249 --> 00:51:05,667
Thank you!

815
00:51:05,750 --> 00:51:07,043
Thank you, everyone!

816
00:51:07,127 --> 00:51:08,420
Here's your certificate.

817
00:51:08,503 --> 00:51:10,005
"President Jang Suk-jin."

818
00:51:10,088 --> 00:51:13,466
"You are hereby appointed president
of the tenants' representative council."

819
00:51:14,050 --> 00:51:15,176
Congratulations.

820
00:51:15,260 --> 00:51:16,845
Thank you.

821
00:51:16,928 --> 00:51:19,806
I got a certificate!

822
00:51:19,890 --> 00:51:21,433
I look forward to working with you.

823
00:51:21,516 --> 00:51:23,393
President Park!

824
00:51:24,019 --> 00:51:25,979
I'll keep doing my best

825
00:51:26,062 --> 00:51:30,108
to love True Value State!

826
00:51:30,191 --> 00:51:32,152
You can love True Value a little less.

827
00:51:32,235 --> 00:51:35,071
No, I love True Value so much.

828
00:51:35,155 --> 00:51:36,740
Look at this, everyone.

829
00:51:37,616 --> 00:51:40,118
Mothers. Oh my gosh.

830
00:51:40,201 --> 00:51:41,286
Hang on.

831
00:51:41,870 --> 00:51:44,831
Congratulations, President Jang.

832
00:51:46,333 --> 00:51:48,084
I'm really sorry about before.

833
00:51:48,168 --> 00:51:52,005
It's fine. I've already put it behind me.

834
00:51:52,631 --> 00:51:55,216
Let's work together from now on.

835
00:51:55,300 --> 00:51:56,217
President Jang!

836
00:51:56,301 --> 00:51:57,844
How about a photo together?

837
00:51:57,928 --> 00:51:59,429
-Gather round.
-Let's take one.

838
00:51:59,512 --> 00:52:00,555
Come here.

839
00:52:00,639 --> 00:52:02,307
All right. Oh gosh!

840
00:52:02,974 --> 00:52:04,100
What?

841
00:52:04,184 --> 00:52:05,143
President Park.

842
00:52:05,894 --> 00:52:08,897
-President Park, you should come here.
-Sorry.

843
00:52:11,566 --> 00:52:12,859
All right, then.

844
00:52:12,943 --> 00:52:14,569
Say "Suk-jin" on the count of three.

845
00:52:15,070 --> 00:52:16,071
Mr. Choi!

846
00:52:16,571 --> 00:52:17,822
One, two, three.

847
00:52:17,906 --> 00:52:19,658
-Suk-jin!
-Suk-jin!

848
00:52:19,741 --> 00:52:21,326
TENANTS' COUNCIL
PRESIDENT JANG SUK-JIN

849
00:52:22,494 --> 00:52:27,165
Walking around our apartment complex
as a president

850
00:52:27,248 --> 00:52:30,210
feels so different.

851
00:52:33,421 --> 00:52:34,506
Damn it.

852
00:52:34,589 --> 00:52:37,133
They always throw trash
in places like this.

853
00:52:37,217 --> 00:52:38,259
Geez.

854
00:52:39,177 --> 00:52:42,013
Ms. Jang, you're a president now.

855
00:52:42,097 --> 00:52:44,057
Maybe you should watch your language…

856
00:52:44,140 --> 00:52:46,184
Oh, you're right.

857
00:52:46,267 --> 00:52:49,813
You're absolutely right.
I should be more cautious now.

858
00:52:52,273 --> 00:52:53,775
But President Park,

859
00:52:53,858 --> 00:52:55,360
I don't care

860
00:52:55,443 --> 00:52:58,321
who you used to be

861
00:52:58,405 --> 00:53:01,908
or what you did in the past anymore.

862
00:53:02,617 --> 00:53:03,451
What?

863
00:53:04,411 --> 00:53:07,497
It doesn't matter
what your intentions were

864
00:53:07,580 --> 00:53:10,667
when you created a fake family

865
00:53:11,459 --> 00:53:14,045
and became the president.

866
00:53:14,629 --> 00:53:16,715
I feel like

867
00:53:16,798 --> 00:53:21,302
you were sent from the heavens
to make this place

868
00:53:21,386 --> 00:53:23,638
a better apartment complex for us.

869
00:53:24,556 --> 00:53:26,516
Isn't that enough?

870
00:53:27,642 --> 00:53:31,604
Where have you been all this time?

871
00:53:32,689 --> 00:53:34,649
Oh gosh. Choco's owner.

872
00:53:34,733 --> 00:53:37,527
He's not cleaning up after his dog again.

873
00:53:37,610 --> 00:53:39,154
He did that last time too.

874
00:53:39,237 --> 00:53:40,196
Choco!

875
00:53:40,280 --> 00:53:41,322
Hey!

876
00:53:41,406 --> 00:53:43,867
You should clean up after your dog!

877
00:53:47,037 --> 00:53:48,621
A better place…

878
00:53:53,960 --> 00:53:55,420
A better place…

879
00:53:56,463 --> 00:53:58,923
ELECTION RESULTS

880
00:54:01,634 --> 00:54:02,886
VERIFYING MY RENTAL UNIT

881
00:54:02,969 --> 00:54:06,347
I told him to reveal the rental units,
and this is what he does?

882
00:54:06,931 --> 00:54:08,975
They're revealing themselves voluntarily.

883
00:54:09,059 --> 00:54:10,226
Does this make any sense?

884
00:54:13,146 --> 00:54:14,731
Is this

885
00:54:14,814 --> 00:54:16,483
Park Hae-kang's magic?

886
00:54:20,945 --> 00:54:22,864
This is entertaining…

887
00:54:23,907 --> 00:54:26,326
but I feel strangely uncomfortable.

888
00:54:36,252 --> 00:54:37,587
I'm home.

889
00:54:43,259 --> 00:54:44,552
I guess she's still working.

890
00:54:49,933 --> 00:54:51,684
What a mess.

891
00:55:16,000 --> 00:55:16,835
What?

892
00:55:17,627 --> 00:55:20,171
Darn it. Ha-jeong's going
to nag me about this.

893
00:55:22,549 --> 00:55:25,343
I always mess up
when I do something I usually don't do.

894
00:55:35,687 --> 00:55:36,604
What is this?

895
00:55:39,190 --> 00:55:41,818
TRANSACTION LEDGER

896
00:55:52,537 --> 00:55:54,372
PARKING GARAGE LIGHT INSPECTION
(NOT CONDUCTED)

897
00:55:54,455 --> 00:55:55,707
WALKWAY CRACK REPAIRS
(REDUCED SCOPE)

898
00:55:55,790 --> 00:55:57,625
EXTERIOR WALL CRACK INSPECTION
(NOT CONDUCTED)

899
00:55:57,709 --> 00:55:59,669
LANDSCAPE PLANTING REPAIRS
(FALSIFIED QUANTITIES)

900
00:56:23,276 --> 00:56:24,152
You…

901
00:56:27,322 --> 00:56:28,531
How did you…

902
00:56:28,615 --> 00:56:30,742
Is this what you were doing
in the management office?

903
00:56:33,077 --> 00:56:35,079
What the hell have you been doing?

904
00:56:37,415 --> 00:56:38,666
It's nothing.

905
00:56:39,167 --> 00:56:40,126
You don't need to know.

906
00:56:40,210 --> 00:56:41,461
It's not nothing.

907
00:56:41,544 --> 00:56:43,630
You supported me
with money you earned like this?

908
00:56:43,713 --> 00:56:44,672
With filthy money?

909
00:56:44,756 --> 00:56:46,716
What's filthy about money?

910
00:56:46,799 --> 00:56:48,593
There's no such thing as filthy money.

911
00:56:48,676 --> 00:56:49,677
Money is just money.

912
00:56:50,303 --> 00:56:51,179
Kang Ha-jeong.

913
00:56:51,763 --> 00:56:55,225
What else could I have done, then?

914
00:56:55,308 --> 00:56:59,145
How could I pay for law school tuition
with my salary?

915
00:57:00,063 --> 00:57:01,856
You said you earned a lot.

916
00:57:01,940 --> 00:57:04,025
You said you had a good salary!

917
00:57:04,108 --> 00:57:06,569
So this is why you were earning a lot.

918
00:57:06,653 --> 00:57:09,572
It was stupid of me to believe you!

919
00:57:10,531 --> 00:57:13,534
You don't need to worry about this.
I'm handling this on my own.

920
00:57:13,618 --> 00:57:14,744
Stop this, right now.

921
00:57:14,827 --> 00:57:17,705
Do you even know
what you've gotten yourself into?

922
00:57:18,289 --> 00:57:20,625
I just did as I was told,

923
00:57:21,376 --> 00:57:22,627
and I was paid for it.

924
00:57:23,378 --> 00:57:24,796
Ha-jeong!

925
00:57:25,296 --> 00:57:29,092
Have you lost your mind? Kang Ha-jeong!

926
00:57:29,801 --> 00:57:30,802
No…

927
00:57:30,885 --> 00:57:33,680
I was the one who was crazy
for eating, sleeping,

928
00:57:33,763 --> 00:57:35,557
and studying with that money.

929
00:57:55,243 --> 00:57:56,953
Mr. Choi…

930
00:57:57,704 --> 00:57:59,372
I'm really sorry,

931
00:58:00,707 --> 00:58:02,458
but I can't do this any longer.

932
00:58:03,876 --> 00:58:05,795
I'm really going to quit now.

933
00:58:05,878 --> 00:58:07,589
So tell Mr. Lee for me.

934
00:58:09,841 --> 00:58:10,883
Ha-jeong.

935
00:58:13,761 --> 00:58:15,638
If you can't do this,

936
00:58:16,264 --> 00:58:18,975
you can accept Mr. Lee's offer.

937
00:58:19,475 --> 00:58:22,103
No, I don't need that.

938
00:58:23,980 --> 00:58:25,315
Let's not do this.

939
00:58:26,482 --> 00:58:27,817
This

940
00:58:27,900 --> 00:58:30,653
could be a matter
of life and death for us.

941
00:58:32,155 --> 00:58:34,282
I'm telling you, I can't do this.

942
00:58:34,949 --> 00:58:36,951
I'm going to pretend I didn't hear this.

943
00:58:39,078 --> 00:58:40,872
I have a ledger.

944
00:58:44,292 --> 00:58:45,168
Ha-jeong.

945
00:58:46,628 --> 00:58:49,422
I recorded everything we've done so far.

946
00:58:54,218 --> 00:58:55,053
If…

947
00:58:56,137 --> 00:58:57,347
If you let me quit,

948
00:58:57,430 --> 00:58:59,057
I'll get rid of the ledger

949
00:58:59,140 --> 00:59:01,309
and live quietly for the rest of my life.

950
00:59:07,482 --> 00:59:09,525
Ha-jeong!

951
00:59:28,169 --> 00:59:31,172
PRESIDENT LEE CHUNG-WON

952
00:59:38,596 --> 00:59:39,514
I…

953
00:59:40,390 --> 00:59:42,016
There's an emergency, sir.

954
00:59:47,146 --> 00:59:49,649
She has a handwritten ledger?

955
00:59:49,732 --> 00:59:50,733
Unbelievable.

956
00:59:51,484 --> 00:59:55,613
So is she thinking of blackmailing me?

957
00:59:57,949 --> 01:00:01,077
She's quite crafty, isn't she?

958
01:00:01,160 --> 01:00:03,705
I really had no idea, sir.

959
01:00:04,747 --> 01:00:07,667
But it doesn't seem
like she has any ill intentions.

960
01:00:08,167 --> 01:00:10,878
If you just allow her to quit…

961
01:00:11,587 --> 01:00:13,214
I can't just leave her be.

962
01:00:13,297 --> 01:00:15,842
She said she'd live quietly if she quit.

963
01:00:15,925 --> 01:00:17,176
And she's trustworthy.

964
01:00:22,014 --> 01:00:24,183
You're so naive, Mr. Choi.

965
01:00:25,601 --> 01:00:26,519
Pardon?

966
01:00:27,270 --> 01:00:30,314
She's been preparing this meticulously
for a long time.

967
01:00:31,733 --> 01:00:33,735
How can you trust someone

968
01:00:33,818 --> 01:00:36,487
who's holding a huge missile in her arms?

969
01:00:38,489 --> 01:00:39,407
She…

970
01:00:39,490 --> 01:00:40,408
She's been

971
01:00:41,409 --> 01:00:43,286
cooperative until now.

972
01:00:44,245 --> 01:00:46,080
She's only asking to quit.

973
01:00:47,331 --> 01:00:48,458
We can trust her.

974
01:00:50,251 --> 01:00:51,127
You know…

975
01:00:53,004 --> 01:00:55,715
I really hate having to wear wet shoes,

976
01:00:56,507 --> 01:00:58,926
not being able to wash my hands
after using the bathroom,

977
01:01:00,011 --> 01:01:03,347
not being able to shower
after working out,

978
01:01:03,431 --> 01:01:05,099
things like that.

979
01:01:05,183 --> 01:01:07,059
I really despise that feeling.

980
01:01:08,060 --> 01:01:09,771
It makes me feel really uneasy.

981
01:01:09,854 --> 01:01:10,855
But right now,

982
01:01:10,938 --> 01:01:13,399
Kang Ha-jeong is making me feel that way.

983
01:01:13,483 --> 01:01:15,359
I feel uneasy.

984
01:01:17,695 --> 01:01:21,115
I feel so uneasy!

985
01:01:23,409 --> 01:01:26,829
ACCOUNTING MANAGER
KANG HA-JEONG

986
01:01:32,794 --> 01:01:33,628
Hey.

987
01:01:34,253 --> 01:01:35,296
Join me.

988
01:01:37,173 --> 01:01:39,008
Come on. Join me.

989
01:01:39,509 --> 01:01:41,886
It's boring doing this alone. Come on.

990
01:01:44,263 --> 01:01:45,223
Sure.

991
01:01:56,484 --> 01:01:59,070
What do you do when you get a hangnail,

992
01:01:59,153 --> 01:02:00,571
Mr. Park?

993
01:02:01,364 --> 01:02:04,116
Do you tear it off, or just leave it?

994
01:02:06,369 --> 01:02:07,203
I tear it off.

995
01:02:08,371 --> 01:02:09,914
I knew it.

996
01:02:09,997 --> 01:02:13,084
I tear it off, even if I start bleeding.
It makes me uneasy.

997
01:02:16,546 --> 01:02:18,130
Can you do something for me?

998
01:02:19,090 --> 01:02:20,341
What is it?

999
01:02:20,925 --> 01:02:23,427
Mr. Kim will contact you later tonight.

1000
01:02:23,511 --> 01:02:26,180
It's nothing special.
You just need to drive.

1001
01:02:26,264 --> 01:02:29,600
Just get in the car
and drive when I tell you to,

1002
01:02:29,684 --> 01:02:31,727
and stop when I tell you to stop.

1003
01:02:31,811 --> 01:02:32,895
It will be easy.

1004
01:02:34,564 --> 01:02:35,773
And when it's over,

1005
01:02:36,774 --> 01:02:38,442
I'll give you the ten billion.

1006
01:02:50,079 --> 01:02:51,289
I'll count on you, then.

1007
01:03:07,763 --> 01:03:10,099
Start the engine and wait inside.

1008
01:03:10,182 --> 01:03:11,601
He'll call you.

1009
01:03:41,339 --> 01:03:42,757
This is Park Hae-kang.

1010
01:03:42,840 --> 01:03:44,467
<i>Yes, I know.</i>

1011
01:03:44,550 --> 01:03:46,969
Of course, I recognize your voice.

1012
01:03:47,053 --> 01:03:49,472
Did you start the car?

1013
01:03:50,181 --> 01:03:51,057
Yes.

1014
01:03:51,641 --> 01:03:52,767
<i>All right.</i>

1015
01:03:52,850 --> 01:03:57,021
Now accelerate gently
and head out onto the main road.

1016
01:04:17,166 --> 01:04:18,626
<i>Good.</i>

1017
01:04:19,251 --> 01:04:20,544
<i>Go straight,</i>

1018
01:04:20,628 --> 01:04:22,546
then turn left into the main road.

1019
01:04:23,547 --> 01:04:25,675
Okay. Turning left.

1020
01:04:30,888 --> 01:04:33,516
Good. You're a good driver.

1021
01:04:34,558 --> 01:04:36,686
It's almost over.

1022
01:04:43,526 --> 01:04:45,319
SHOULD WE HAVE SPICY RICE CAKES LATER?

1023
01:04:48,406 --> 01:04:52,827
<i>Why don't you start</i>
<i>increasing the speed now?</i>

1024
01:05:02,128 --> 01:05:06,007
<i>There's going to be a bus stop</i>
<i>about 300 meters in front of you.</i>

1025
01:05:06,090 --> 01:05:07,508
<i>Do you see it?</i>

1026
01:05:07,591 --> 01:05:08,634
Yes, I see it.

1027
01:05:08,718 --> 01:05:10,511
Crash into the woman

1028
01:05:10,594 --> 01:05:12,388
standing there!

1029
01:06:07,276 --> 01:06:08,527
Park Hae-kang…

1030
01:06:12,323 --> 01:06:13,324
All right.

1031
01:06:13,991 --> 01:06:15,493
I'm coming to you.

1032
01:06:37,098 --> 01:06:38,224
This is ten billion won.

1033
01:06:39,058 --> 01:06:41,769
I told you I'd give you the money
once you did this.

1034
01:06:42,353 --> 01:06:44,897
You can save your old boss
with this money.

1035
01:06:44,980 --> 01:06:47,858
You shouldn't leave him there
when he's already sick.

1036
01:06:48,484 --> 01:06:50,444
All you had to do

1037
01:06:50,528 --> 01:06:52,738
was crash into a woman
standing right there.

1038
01:06:53,364 --> 01:06:55,074
You've pulled off harder things than that,

1039
01:06:55,157 --> 01:06:58,410
but you fail to do the easiest job?

1040
01:07:00,329 --> 01:07:01,914
I may be a bad guy,

1041
01:07:02,790 --> 01:07:04,458
but you're just trash.

1042
01:07:05,042 --> 01:07:06,544
Trash?

1043
01:07:07,294 --> 01:07:10,422
You're being quite rude to a guy

1044
01:07:11,590 --> 01:07:12,842
who's interested in you.

1045
01:07:13,676 --> 01:07:15,344
I don't date trash.

1046
01:07:18,180 --> 01:07:20,391
Then what will you do with me?

1047
01:07:21,308 --> 01:07:22,518
I think

1048
01:07:23,227 --> 01:07:25,688
I can make things
very interesting for you.

1049
01:07:36,198 --> 01:07:38,909
THE APARTMENT JOB

1050
01:08:03,017 --> 01:08:05,561
I would like to suggest a safety patrol.

1051
01:08:05,644 --> 01:08:08,480
<i>We should show everyone</i>
<i>that we're the ones</i>

1052
01:08:08,564 --> 01:08:11,400
<i>who care the most about this place.</i>

1053
01:08:11,483 --> 01:08:13,194
Goodness. What is all this?

1054
01:08:13,277 --> 01:08:14,820
<i>That's Gyeong-buk's kindergarten.</i>

1055
01:08:14,904 --> 01:08:16,530
<i>President Park, we need you to step up.</i>

1056
01:08:16,614 --> 01:08:18,240
<i>Of course,</i>
<i>I should step up as the president.</i>

1057
01:08:18,324 --> 01:08:21,202
Has the building really aged this fast?

1058
01:08:21,285 --> 01:08:22,870
No, it's shoddy construction.

1059
01:08:22,953 --> 01:08:24,914
<i>President Park's wife?</i>

1060
01:08:24,997 --> 01:08:26,874
<i>So it's you. You tried to kill my sister.</i>

1061
01:08:26,957 --> 01:08:28,125
<i>How about 500 million?</i>

1062
01:08:28,209 --> 01:08:30,961
I'm sure that's more than what you got
for playing Park Hae-kang's wife.

1063
01:08:31,045 --> 01:08:32,171
<i>If you want him released…</i>

1064
01:08:32,254 --> 01:08:33,839
<i>Police! Open the door.</i>

1065
01:08:33,923 --> 01:08:35,507
<i>…bring me the ledger.</i>

1066
01:08:35,591 --> 01:08:37,218
Simple, isn't it?

1067
01:08:37,301 --> 01:08:40,387
<i>It's not something you can handle.</i>
<i>Hand it over to me.</i>

1068
01:08:40,471 --> 01:08:41,764
<i>I can't hand it over.</i>

1069
01:08:44,808 --> 01:08:46,810
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park

